1
00:00:00,806 --> 00:00:09,975
[SPEAKER_04]: Okay, good evening and welcome to the Tufts University pre-application community meeting regarding our new tennis courts.

2
00:00:10,715 --> 00:00:12,217
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you for joining us tonight.

3
00:00:13,738 --> 00:00:19,403
[SPEAKER_04]: We really appreciate being able to present this to you and hearing your feedback and answering your questions.

4
00:00:20,905 --> 00:00:26,149
[SPEAKER_04]: Tonight's meeting is being recorded and will be uploaded to our website next week.

5
00:00:27,212 --> 00:00:32,053
[SPEAKER_04]: My name is Rocco DiRico and I'm the Executive Director of Government and Community Relations at Tufts University.

6
00:00:32,934 --> 00:00:40,396
[SPEAKER_04]: We are here tonight to discuss our proposal to add eight new tennis courts to Field A on College Avenue in Medford.

7
00:00:40,976 --> 00:00:44,257
[SPEAKER_04]: Field A is adjacent to the parking lot across from Cousins Gym.

8
00:00:45,537 --> 00:00:53,939
[SPEAKER_04]: The current tennis courts that we have are located on Professor's Row and have been used for student housing for the past two years.

9
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:55,440
[SPEAKER_04]: We placed

10
00:00:57,001 --> 00:01:05,568
[SPEAKER_04]: modular housing units on the courts to isolate COVID positive students during the pandemic.

11
00:01:06,269 --> 00:01:09,232
[SPEAKER_04]: And we discovered it was actually a good location for housing.

12
00:01:10,513 --> 00:01:20,361
[SPEAKER_04]: So going forward, those courts will continue to be used for housing where it can currently constructing temporarily housing units for first year students on those courts.

13
00:01:21,634 --> 00:01:27,096
[SPEAKER_04]: This will allow us to house more students on campus, which I know is a goal of both the university and the city.

14
00:01:28,957 --> 00:01:37,420
[SPEAKER_04]: The site there is much more suitable for housing because it's closer to our academic buildings, our cafeterias and other dormitories.

15
00:01:38,597 --> 00:01:51,705
[SPEAKER_04]: This location that we're proposing for the tennis courts tonight is more appropriate for tennis courts as it's adjacent to our existing athletics facilities for baseball, softball, lacrosse, and intramural sports.

16
00:01:52,606 --> 00:01:58,370
[SPEAKER_04]: It's also directly across the street from the Gantra Center, the Tisch Fitness Center, Cousins Gym, and our locker rooms.

17
00:01:59,606 --> 00:02:02,469
[SPEAKER_04]: At this meeting you'll hear from our athletic director john Morris.

18
00:02:03,671 --> 00:02:08,256
[SPEAKER_04]: Next, the project manager Jen Whitney will walk you through the project.

19
00:02:08,917 --> 00:02:13,542
[SPEAKER_04]: You'll also hear from john Hickok from CHA, who is our architect.

20
00:02:14,571 --> 00:02:16,412
[SPEAKER_04]: And finally, we'll take your questions.

21
00:02:17,212 --> 00:02:23,415
[SPEAKER_04]: Leah Boudreau from my office will read through the questions that have been pre-submitted.

22
00:02:23,435 --> 00:02:29,458
[SPEAKER_04]: We'll answer those first, and then we'll go to questions that are submitted in the Q&A.

23
00:02:30,539 --> 00:02:35,981
[SPEAKER_04]: To ask a question tonight, please use the Q&A button located at the bottom of your screen.

24
00:02:36,962 --> 00:02:41,244
[SPEAKER_04]: If we don't get to your question tonight, please contact our office at any time.

25
00:02:42,097 --> 00:02:52,704
[SPEAKER_04]: at 617-627-3780 or by emailing us at communityrelations at tufts.edu.

26
00:02:53,685 --> 00:02:56,346
[SPEAKER_04]: I wanna thank Victor Schrader from the city of Medford.

27
00:02:56,827 --> 00:03:01,910
[SPEAKER_04]: Victor is the city's director of economic development and is here tonight representing Mayor Longo Kern.

28
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:08,034
[SPEAKER_04]: I also wanna thank Mark Maggiore and Andy Colbert for their technical support tonight behind the scenes.

29
00:03:09,212 --> 00:03:14,174
[SPEAKER_04]: And with that, please welcome Tufts University Athletic Director, John Morris.

30
00:03:16,175 --> 00:03:16,796
[SPEAKER_01]: Thanks Rocco.

31
00:03:17,696 --> 00:03:24,499
[SPEAKER_01]: And thanks everyone for being with us this evening and for your interest in hearing more about this project that I'm really excited.

32
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:32,083
[SPEAKER_01]: First, let me say normally for an important meeting like this, I would have worn a sport coat.

33
00:03:32,383 --> 00:03:33,724
[SPEAKER_01]: I just left it at home.

34
00:03:34,164 --> 00:03:36,325
[SPEAKER_01]: It was sitting right by the back door and I left it.

35
00:03:36,702 --> 00:03:40,465
[SPEAKER_01]: I ran down the hall a few minutes ago right before this started to try to see if I could find one.

36
00:03:40,505 --> 00:03:45,008
[SPEAKER_01]: The only one I could find was our football coaches and it was about nine sizes too big.

37
00:03:45,088 --> 00:03:47,310
[SPEAKER_01]: So I thought it would be better to go without.

38
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:50,412
[SPEAKER_01]: But anyway, I'm really excited about this project.

39
00:03:50,732 --> 00:03:57,597
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll spare you the detail and just share a couple of things that, a couple of the reasons why I am excited.

40
00:03:59,179 --> 00:04:04,062
[SPEAKER_01]: Like all our projects, we try to make them beneficial to as many groups as possible.

41
00:04:04,563 --> 00:04:04,943
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's,

42
00:04:06,007 --> 00:04:07,428
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why I'm excited about this one.

43
00:04:07,488 --> 00:04:13,610
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course, it will benefit our varsity tennis teams to have a varsity course here.

44
00:04:14,511 --> 00:04:20,353
[SPEAKER_01]: But I'm excited because it's also gonna benefit the whole Tufts community, faculty, staff, everyone.

45
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:30,638
[SPEAKER_01]: Just another opportunity to get outside and work on fitness, recreation, and health and wellbeing.

46
00:04:31,718 --> 00:04:35,300
[SPEAKER_01]: But also, I think it's gonna benefit the Medford community.

47
00:04:36,188 --> 00:04:39,932
[SPEAKER_01]: We're really excited about this course being available to Medford residents.

48
00:04:41,394 --> 00:04:48,141
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course, when our varsity teams are practicing or competing or teaching a PE class of some kind on the course, they won't be.

49
00:04:48,562 --> 00:04:56,350
[SPEAKER_01]: But generally speaking, the course that we had up on top of the hill, our community, local community members use them frequently.

50
00:04:57,098 --> 00:05:09,652
[SPEAKER_01]: So we're excited that this will be another way for us to partner with Medford and allow the local residents to use the courts and and get that same type of physical fitness, another option for that.

51
00:05:11,073 --> 00:05:14,517
[SPEAKER_01]: Another reason I'm really excited about it and Rocco alluded to it was just the.

52
00:05:15,305 --> 00:05:17,606
[SPEAKER_01]: proximity to the rest of our athletics facilities.

53
00:05:17,686 --> 00:05:24,848
[SPEAKER_01]: I think it's going to be a lot more meaningful for our tennis athletes to feel more a part of the rest of our athletics community.

54
00:05:24,868 --> 00:05:35,171
[SPEAKER_01]: I think students and faculty and staff using the courts, the convenience of having the locker rooms nearby and access to the fitness center just makes sense that it's all there.

55
00:05:36,671 --> 00:05:39,432
[SPEAKER_01]: So we're really excited about it from that standpoint, too.

56
00:05:39,472 --> 00:05:42,673
[SPEAKER_01]: We think it's going to be a great addition to the whole athletics physical plan.

57
00:05:44,884 --> 00:05:53,947
[SPEAKER_01]: Those are the reasons I'm really excited about it and look forward to helping answer any questions you may have about the project later in the program.

58
00:05:54,387 --> 00:06:01,769
[SPEAKER_01]: For now, I will kick it over to Jen Whitney, who will show you some images and walk you through those specifics of the project.

59
00:06:06,971 --> 00:06:07,851
[SPEAKER_05]: Good evening, everyone.

60
00:06:07,931 --> 00:06:10,692
[SPEAKER_06]: Thank you for allowing me to present this project.

61
