68
00:06:58,394 --> 00:07:07,558
[SPEAKER_06]: As Rocco mentioned, on the existing conditions, we currently are housing our COVID positive modular

69
00:07:08,148 --> 00:07:13,552
[SPEAKER_06]: isolation unit on the current courts located on Professor's Row.

70
00:07:14,273 --> 00:07:31,026
[SPEAKER_06]: And there is, as we've discovered, it's a much better location for residential facilities and have done quite a few studies to move this down to the athletics corridor to bring everything together.

71
00:07:31,046 --> 00:07:32,808
[SPEAKER_06]: Next slide, please.

72
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:45,883
[SPEAKER_06]: So just some highlights about the tennis construction, proposing to relocate the tennis complex to the alumni field, as indicated in the previous slide.

73
00:07:46,863 --> 00:07:51,545
[SPEAKER_06]: There's a total of eight new concrete courts with an acrylic surface planned.

74
00:07:52,285 --> 00:07:57,126
[SPEAKER_06]: And this is a much more durable surface, requires a lot less often resurfacing.

75
00:07:57,146 --> 00:07:58,447
[SPEAKER_06]: Some new scoreboards,

76
00:08:03,182 --> 00:08:21,231
[SPEAKER_06]: some temporary spectator seating, new state-of-the-art LED sports lighting, and then landscape screening around the perimeter, very focused around the adjacent homes.

77
