171
00:20:19,481 --> 00:20:25,846
[SPEAKER_01]: Maybe some youth tennis clinics, things like that, other ways to let the local residents benefit from the courts.

172
00:20:29,068 --> 00:20:29,909
[SPEAKER_00]: Thanks, John, very much.

173
00:20:31,430 --> 00:20:36,894
[SPEAKER_00]: We've got another question or a series of questions from Judy Weinstock regarding lighting.

174
00:20:38,479 --> 00:20:39,680
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll go ahead and read those.

175
00:20:40,881 --> 00:20:47,064
[SPEAKER_00]: Judy says, I remain concerned about the larger plan that Tufts has related to light filtration and pollution.

176
00:20:47,765 --> 00:20:57,730
[SPEAKER_00]: As project numbers such as the Tennis Courts project increase, so does light pollution on abutting properties that spills into the neighborhoods and homes.

177
00:20:59,121 --> 00:21:07,283
[SPEAKER_00]: I would like to hear specifically about how Tufts will mitigate future light pollution as it relates to both this project and sport field improvement projects.

178
00:21:07,803 --> 00:21:10,504
[SPEAKER_00]: How will new lighting be different from existing lighting?

179
00:21:10,744 --> 00:21:12,724
[SPEAKER_00]: And when will fields be illuminated?

180
00:21:13,164 --> 00:21:15,725
[SPEAKER_00]: And will there be auto shut off time periods?

181
00:21:16,445 --> 00:21:20,626
[SPEAKER_00]: Will fields and courts be illuminated after dark on a routine basis?

182
00:21:21,146 --> 00:21:22,927
[SPEAKER_00]: And will some form of lighting be on 24-7?

183
00:21:25,684 --> 00:21:34,748
[SPEAKER_00]: John Hickok, if you could address some of Judy's questions about lighting, light pollution, and timing, that would be great.

184
00:21:35,629 --> 00:21:36,669
[SPEAKER_02]: Sure.

185
00:21:36,789 --> 00:21:47,374
[SPEAKER_02]: As I stated in the previous slide, that was one of our charges of the project was to make that corner of the property better for the adjoining neighbors.

186
00:21:48,255 --> 00:21:57,519
[SPEAKER_02]: So we, as I had indicated, we employed state-of-the-art LED technology for lighting of these tennis courts to allow for nighttime play.

187
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:02,021
[SPEAKER_02]: The lights, as I indicated, are highly programmable.

188
00:22:02,101 --> 00:22:07,303
[SPEAKER_02]: So the athletics and the university have control of when the lights come on, when the lights go off.

189
00:22:08,163 --> 00:22:16,586
[SPEAKER_02]: And they have additional controls through authorized users for mobile devices and things of that nature to also turn lights on, turn lights off.

190
00:22:19,685 --> 00:22:25,026
[SPEAKER_02]: I showed the graphic of the lighting of how we've minimized that spill to the neighborhood.

191
00:22:25,126 --> 00:22:36,328
[SPEAKER_02]: And like I said, it was one of our charges to do that and make this so that it can be an asset to the community and not a detriment.

192
00:22:36,348 --> 00:22:47,010
[SPEAKER_02]: And I feel that the design has really taken hold there and really made this better by removing that very old technology

193
00:22:48,041 --> 00:22:55,185
[SPEAKER_02]: that allows for a lot of spillage to happen beyond the actual surface that's being played on.

194
00:22:55,565 --> 00:23:04,710
[SPEAKER_02]: As it relates to the timing and when the lights will be on, I'll turn that over to John Morris and allow him to talk to that.

195
00:23:06,711 --> 00:23:06,951
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

196
00:23:06,991 --> 00:23:08,472
[SPEAKER_01]: Thanks, John.

197
00:23:11,314 --> 00:23:13,635
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, they absolutely will not be on 24-7.

198
00:23:14,435 --> 00:23:17,397
[SPEAKER_01]: We will make sure to follow all the Medford

199
00:23:18,650 --> 00:23:25,356
[SPEAKER_01]: regulations about when lights can be on consistent with what we've done out at the other fields in that area.

200
00:23:25,396 --> 00:23:27,677
[SPEAKER_01]: I believe Medford requires a 10 p.m.

201
00:23:27,718 --> 00:23:28,098
[SPEAKER_01]: shutoff.

202
00:23:29,099 --> 00:23:30,680
[SPEAKER_01]: We will monitor really closely.

203
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:34,583
[SPEAKER_01]: We will program it so that it turns off in a timely manner.

204
00:23:36,565 --> 00:23:39,407
[SPEAKER_01]: And, you know, in the winter, I don't imagine that being on much at all.

205
00:23:39,447 --> 00:23:42,830
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't see the tennis courts being in use in the winter.

206
00:23:42,890 --> 00:23:44,371
[SPEAKER_01]: I think it'll be a spring, summer,

207
00:23:45,278 --> 00:23:46,139
[SPEAKER_01]: and fall thing.

208
00:23:46,379 --> 00:23:50,562
[SPEAKER_01]: And for most of the summer and early fall, it stays light, pretty light anyway.

209
00:23:50,582 --> 00:23:55,966
[SPEAKER_01]: So hopefully it won't be too much of an impact during those times.

210
00:23:56,086 --> 00:24:03,151
[SPEAKER_01]: And then I guess I'd also just say that we wanna work with Rocco's office and monitor it closely.

211
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:10,616
[SPEAKER_01]: If there really isn't any usage going on, but after nine, we'll just adjust and shut them off at nine.

212
00:24:11,777 --> 00:24:14,479
[SPEAKER_01]: And Rocco can probably speak to this better than I can.

213
00:24:15,683 --> 00:24:30,607
[SPEAKER_01]: But yeah, we will program them so they automatically turn off, but we'll also publish ways that if there is an isolated mistake or maybe it doesn't turn off one night if they're on later than the time, ways to call into TUPD or otherwise.

214
00:24:30,847 --> 00:24:32,068
[SPEAKER_01]: Rocco, I don't want to screw this up.

215
00:24:32,108 --> 00:24:33,408
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll let you handle that part.

216
00:24:33,448 --> 00:24:37,469
[SPEAKER_01]: But there are ways that neighbors can report it and we can get them turned off immediately.

217
00:24:39,243 --> 00:24:57,440
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you john yeah for any issues during normal work hours obviously just contact our office 617-627-3780, or community relations at Tufts.edu if as john said there's a, the light is on and it's past 10 o'clock on a Wednesday night for some reason.

218
00:24:58,400 --> 00:25:09,785
[SPEAKER_04]: TUPD, their phone number is on 24 seven, and you can always call them and then they can program the lights remotely.

219
00:25:10,966 --> 00:25:16,268
[SPEAKER_04]: So we have a number of ways to get in touch with us should any issues arise when the courts are operational.

220
00:25:19,945 --> 00:25:20,685
[SPEAKER_00]: Thanks Rocco.

221
00:25:21,306 --> 00:25:29,371
[SPEAKER_00]: Just one more pre submitted question from Janice Rosansky Janice asks, will there be a backboard with the tennis courts.

222
00:25:31,132 --> 00:25:35,334
[SPEAKER_00]: John could you john Morris, could you address Janice's question about about backboards.

223
00:25:36,115 --> 00:25:41,878
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure, um, we, the current design does not have a backboard in it at all.

224
00:25:42,779 --> 00:25:46,101
[SPEAKER_01]: But full transparency, it's something that we're still talking about.

225
00:25:47,909 --> 00:25:50,231
[SPEAKER_01]: Our coaches have a little bit of interest in it.

226
00:25:51,032 --> 00:25:55,636
[SPEAKER_01]: And sometimes it is nice for a person to be able to go out and kind of warm up by herself or himself.

227
00:25:55,756 --> 00:26:02,942
[SPEAKER_01]: But at this point, we don't have a hitting wall or backboard in the design.

228
00:26:03,242 --> 00:26:14,012
[SPEAKER_01]: But I will say this, if we were to do it, again, because I'm trying to think about how to do it in a way that's as least impactful to the neighborhood as possible,

229
00:26:15,050 --> 00:26:17,552
[SPEAKER_01]: We would not put one up made of wood.

230
00:26:17,612 --> 00:26:21,494
[SPEAKER_01]: Those are really loud and they make a lot of noise.

231
00:26:21,574 --> 00:26:29,859
[SPEAKER_01]: If we did it, we would do more of a block wall that is really sound absorbent and wouldn't create that kind of annoying repetitive noise.

232
00:26:29,939 --> 00:26:33,281
[SPEAKER_01]: The wall would really absorb any noise if we were to do it.

233
00:26:38,890 --> 00:26:39,650
[SPEAKER_00]: Thank you, John.

234
00:26:40,110 --> 00:26:42,571
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's it for pre-submitted questions.

235
00:26:43,991 --> 00:26:49,613
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll go ahead and pass it back to Rocco, who's going to moderate some of the questions that have been coming in via the chat.

236
00:26:51,213 --> 00:26:51,934
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, Leah.

237
00:26:52,274 --> 00:26:54,934
[SPEAKER_04]: And the first question comes from Evan Kreshtul.

238
00:26:56,495 --> 00:26:58,775
[SPEAKER_04]: John Morris, if you could answer this one.

239
00:26:59,896 --> 00:27:07,038
[SPEAKER_04]: If the court is allowed to be used by the community as a whole, can we please allow for an additional entrance to the courts?

240
00:27:08,103 --> 00:27:14,266
[SPEAKER_04]: Perhaps along Fleming Street or Buzzle Lane, there is an existing entrance there that is always locked.

241
00:27:19,548 --> 00:27:22,649
[SPEAKER_01]: Rocko, I may have to answer that one with you and drag you back into that.

242
00:27:22,809 --> 00:27:26,631
[SPEAKER_01]: But this comment has come up before.

243
00:27:27,331 --> 00:27:31,833
[SPEAKER_01]: And I believe we've talked to TUPD, Rocko, correct me if I'm wrong.

244
00:27:32,293 --> 00:27:35,794
[SPEAKER_01]: And we are open to opening those gates.

245
00:27:38,063 --> 00:27:44,345
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that the current plan is to possibly wait for the T to open to get those going.

246
00:27:44,425 --> 00:27:51,087
[SPEAKER_01]: But so maybe Rocco, you may have more information than I do about timing, but the answer to the question is yes.

247
00:27:51,787 --> 00:27:54,348
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just a question of when we open those gates.

248
00:27:54,588 --> 00:27:55,548
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you agree with that Rocco?

249
00:27:55,568 --> 00:27:57,769
[SPEAKER_01]: I want to make sure I'm not giving inaccurate information.

250
00:27:57,789 --> 00:27:59,850
[SPEAKER_01]: I think philosophically, we're very open to it.

251
00:27:59,910 --> 00:28:00,510
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just when.

252
00:28:01,445 --> 00:28:05,928
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah john Thank you very much and yeah as john say that athletics has signed off on it.

253
00:28:06,889 --> 00:28:20,339
[SPEAKER_04]: We've also spoken to facilities and the Tufts University Police Department, and they are okay with the idea, there has been a suggestion to wait, particularly while so much construction is going on this summer.

254
00:28:21,219 --> 00:28:24,382
[SPEAKER_04]: And while we're waiting for the green line to open so.

255
00:28:25,042 --> 00:28:36,829
[SPEAKER_04]: during construction that gate may be closed but post-construction and with the opening of the green line expected in late summer that's where we're going to time it to unlock it.

256
00:28:37,369 --> 00:28:52,638
[SPEAKER_04]: I was actually out on the fields today and I know that there is a gate on Wellesley Street and that is open and accessible for neighbors but the gate at the end of this street we can certainly look at again

257
00:28:53,679 --> 00:29:05,130
[SPEAKER_04]: Perhaps when construction is complete in that area and it's safe to walk through, and when the green lines open to give folks better access to the new Medford Tufts station.

258
00:29:06,491 --> 00:29:12,257
[SPEAKER_04]: The next question is also from Evan, and I think I'm going to ask Jen to answer this one.

259
00:29:13,078 --> 00:29:19,862
[SPEAKER_04]: How much of Field A or the alumni fields in general will be cut off and unusable during construction?

260
00:29:20,703 --> 00:29:32,950
[SPEAKER_04]: Fall 22 through June 23 is a bulk of a full year and Field A is used year round by both Tufts and surrounding community members for tons of activities.

261
00:29:34,787 --> 00:29:35,887
[SPEAKER_06]: I'm happy to take that one.

262
00:29:36,287 --> 00:29:51,612
[SPEAKER_06]: So initially during the construction period that we start here in the fall, we would probably utilize a good portion of Field A to sort of lay down access and prep that area.

263
00:29:52,752 --> 00:30:00,315
[SPEAKER_06]: So Field A would probably be out of commission for the good portion of the fall construction and

264
00:30:01,298 --> 00:30:24,104
[SPEAKER_06]: we would be tightening up as we would complete the construction here in the fall with the concrete and the fencing and whatnot and tighten up the site and restore the remainder that won't have the tennis on it to restore that for the fall after we tighten up the site.

265
00:30:24,544 --> 00:30:26,445
[SPEAKER_06]: And then come spring, that

266
00:30:27,927 --> 00:30:30,008
[SPEAKER_06]: you know, that could be utilized next to it.

267
00:30:30,068 --> 00:30:42,256
[SPEAKER_06]: But it will grow and then it will contract as the construction needs, because we'll need to utilize that area for lay down and access to construct the tennis courts.

268
00:30:44,678 --> 00:30:45,679
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, Jen.

269
00:30:46,019 --> 00:30:49,101
[SPEAKER_04]: And the next question is for John Morris.

270
00:30:50,122 --> 00:30:51,462
[SPEAKER_04]: This is from Dave Katz.

271
00:30:52,023 --> 00:30:55,025
[SPEAKER_04]: Can community members access the Tisch Fitness Center?

272
00:30:56,594 --> 00:30:59,476
[SPEAKER_01]: I want to be moderator next time, so I can just kick them to everybody.

273
00:30:59,496 --> 00:31:03,398
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry, Rocco.

274
00:31:04,039 --> 00:31:08,342
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, the candid answer to that one is yes and no.

275
00:31:10,483 --> 00:31:25,833
[SPEAKER_01]: Currently, because of COVID, and it's been this way, unfortunately, for a couple of years, the Tisch Fitness Center has not been open to anyone other than the Tufts community, faculty, staff, and students prior to COVID.

276
00:31:26,723 --> 00:31:36,708
[SPEAKER_01]: The Tisch Fitness Center was open to abutters, the list of neighbors who abut the property and there's, Rocco can explain where that list is.

277
00:31:37,509 --> 00:31:46,133
[SPEAKER_01]: And also we made it open to the Medford first responders.

278
00:31:47,414 --> 00:31:53,737
[SPEAKER_01]: The good news I do have for you though, is that the, we have been all summer, we wanna get it open again.

279
00:31:54,208 --> 00:31:59,652
[SPEAKER_01]: for the Medford abutters who live in the neighborhood and are on the list of folks who can use it.

280
00:32:00,273 --> 00:32:04,095
[SPEAKER_01]: And we've been kind of nudging our medical staff in that direction.

281
00:32:04,116 --> 00:32:12,562
[SPEAKER_01]: And I wish I had a firm date for you, but we did get the approval, which is great news to reopen the Tisch Center for the abutters.

282
00:32:13,382 --> 00:32:14,984
[SPEAKER_01]: And it'll be this fall.

283
00:32:15,004 --> 00:32:18,549
[SPEAKER_01]: Will that be September 1, August 15, September 15?

284
00:32:18,609 --> 00:32:19,550
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not exactly sure.

285
00:32:20,291 --> 00:32:21,533
[SPEAKER_01]: We're working on that now.

286
00:32:23,175 --> 00:32:24,416
[SPEAKER_01]: But it will be this fall.

287
00:32:25,438 --> 00:32:26,419
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'm excited about that.

288
00:32:26,459 --> 00:32:27,040
[SPEAKER_01]: That's good news.

289
00:32:28,121 --> 00:32:46,689
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, thank you very much john and once that once we are able to open it back up to a butters we will share that information with our neighbors on our website, and by other means and as john said, there's a list of budding streets that will go along with that that show who's eligible for it.

290
00:32:47,809 --> 00:32:53,952
[SPEAKER_04]: And as john mentioned, there was a previous agreement as well that Medford police officers and firefighters.

291
00:32:55,273 --> 00:32:56,594
[SPEAKER_04]: can use the facility as well.

292
00:32:56,994 --> 00:32:58,415
[SPEAKER_04]: You do have to pay for the pass.

293
00:32:58,475 --> 00:33:00,057
[SPEAKER_04]: I do want to be clear for that.

294
00:33:00,097 --> 00:33:03,520
[SPEAKER_04]: You do have to pay for an abutter's pass to utilize it.

295
00:33:05,361 --> 00:33:11,427
[SPEAKER_04]: But I know it was a popular program pre-pandemic and as John said, now that we're

296
00:33:12,093 --> 00:33:14,714
[SPEAKER_04]: entering a new phase of the pandemic, or hopefully coming out of it.

297
00:33:15,114 --> 00:33:17,874
[SPEAKER_04]: We look forward to offering that program again.

298
00:33:17,894 --> 00:33:22,455
[SPEAKER_04]: The next question is also from Dave Katz.

299
00:33:23,536 --> 00:33:27,857
[SPEAKER_04]: And this question is probably for John Moore.

300
00:33:27,877 --> 00:33:28,977
[SPEAKER_04]: Sorry, John, we're going to you again.

301
00:33:29,897 --> 00:33:34,898
[SPEAKER_04]: But will there be a bubble or any winter use of the courts?

302
00:33:36,279 --> 00:33:37,839
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm in athletics, so I like to win.

303
00:33:37,899 --> 00:33:39,420
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'm getting most of the questions.

304
00:33:39,440 --> 00:33:40,400
[SPEAKER_01]: So I feel like I'm winning.

305
00:33:41,894 --> 00:33:43,195
[SPEAKER_01]: No, there will not be a bubble.

306
00:33:43,235 --> 00:33:44,556
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no plan for a bubble.

307
00:33:44,596 --> 00:33:46,818
[SPEAKER_01]: I know Harvard and BC have done those.

308
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:54,105
[SPEAKER_01]: Those are really expensive to buy, really expensive to maintain, not great to look at, and expensive to store.

309
00:33:54,345 --> 00:33:56,587
[SPEAKER_01]: So no bubble, no bubble out there.

310
00:33:56,827 --> 00:33:59,729
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, it would be, in a way, it would be nice.

311
00:34:00,030 --> 00:34:03,373
[SPEAKER_01]: I suspect some people would like it because then it could be used in the winter.

312
00:34:04,494 --> 00:34:06,115
[SPEAKER_01]: But no plans to do a bubble.

313
00:34:07,630 --> 00:34:08,311
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, John.

314
00:34:09,291 --> 00:34:11,553
[SPEAKER_04]: And Jen, this next question is for you.

315
00:34:12,414 --> 00:34:14,515
[SPEAKER_04]: And I do think you touched on this earlier in the meeting.

316
00:34:14,575 --> 00:34:18,719
[SPEAKER_04]: But if you could just reiterate, this question comes from Sharon Wong.

317
00:34:19,419 --> 00:34:23,722
[SPEAKER_04]: I may have missed this in the beginning of the meeting, but when will the courts be completed?

318
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:30,808
[SPEAKER_06]: So the plan is to have the courts open for use right about this time next year.

319
00:34:30,888 --> 00:34:37,073
[SPEAKER_06]: We'll start in the fall getting construction going once we're permitted with the city

320
00:34:37,558 --> 00:34:41,000
[SPEAKER_06]: and procure all of our materials to begin construction.

321
00:34:41,601 --> 00:34:50,827
[SPEAKER_06]: There's a waiting period for the concrete and we have to wait until until spring to then coat.

322
00:34:51,347 --> 00:34:57,992
[SPEAKER_06]: So the timing around this pushed our project into the spring when we have warmer temperatures to put the acrylic surface on.

323
00:34:58,492 --> 00:35:06,838
[SPEAKER_06]: But the long story short is next June, end of June, we're going to be playing tennis on those courts.

324
00:35:09,338 --> 00:35:19,341
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you very much, Jen, and I will take this question, because I think it's it's touched on something we've talked about earlier.

325
00:35:20,542 --> 00:35:20,902
[SPEAKER_04]: This one.

326
00:35:21,622 --> 00:35:33,666
[SPEAKER_04]: There's no name attached to it just comes from 446215, but it's will you be opening up the end of Wellesley Street that intersects with Colby Street during this project.

327
00:35:35,287 --> 00:35:43,510
[SPEAKER_04]: So Wellesley Street actually does as it exists right now connect to Colby Street.

328
00:35:44,550 --> 00:35:57,394
[SPEAKER_04]: And you can go down to the end of Colby Street, and there is a walkway that takes you eventually to College Avenue, so that that area is open actually right now, and will remain open.

329
00:35:59,175 --> 00:36:08,658
[SPEAKER_04]: To answer if this is similar to the question that was before about the fencing, there is an existing gate on Wellesley Street.

330
00:36:09,178 --> 00:36:15,640
[SPEAKER_04]: I was actually on the fields this afternoon and neighbors were going in and out of there.

331
00:36:16,981 --> 00:36:20,902
[SPEAKER_04]: So that gate is right now open and unlocked.

332
00:36:22,302 --> 00:36:27,324
[SPEAKER_04]: So I don't anticipate that that will be closed because there's no construction happening in that

333
00:36:27,964 --> 00:36:29,124
[SPEAKER_04]: immediate area.

334
00:36:30,244 --> 00:36:40,186
[SPEAKER_04]: And as John alluded to earlier, we're going to try to figure out ways to make the fields more accessible in anticipation of the green line coming in late summer.

335
00:36:42,827 --> 00:36:47,287
[SPEAKER_04]: So those are all the questions that have been pre-submitted.

336
00:36:47,307 --> 00:36:55,329
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm happy to pass it off to Victor from the city, just in case he has any questions.

337
00:36:57,776 --> 00:37:01,280
[SPEAKER_04]: So I'll give Victor an opportunity to speak here, and then we'll go from there.

338
00:37:04,062 --> 00:37:04,663
[SPEAKER_03]: Thanks Rocco.

339
00:37:04,703 --> 00:37:05,824
[SPEAKER_03]: Good evening, everyone.

340
00:37:05,864 --> 00:37:09,368
[SPEAKER_03]: Thanks for attending and submitting your questions.

341
00:37:09,928 --> 00:37:13,692
[SPEAKER_03]: Thank you to Tufts for holding this pre-application community meeting.

342
00:37:13,752 --> 00:37:14,333
[SPEAKER_03]: We're asking

343
00:37:15,695 --> 00:37:35,323
[SPEAKER_03]: Tufts community partners developers to host these meetings before they apply so that we can hear from residents gather questions and concerns and make sure they're addressed as these projects go through permitting, so thank you for submitting your questions and concerns and I'm taking note and we'll pass them along to the relevant departments.

344
00:37:37,008 --> 00:37:43,431
[SPEAKER_03]: Rock, I just wanted to add that this meeting will also be posted on Medford Community Media.

345
00:37:43,511 --> 00:37:57,676
[SPEAKER_03]: Tufts will share the recording with us so folks can go back and watch it, watch that recording after the fact or tell your neighbors and they can watch it on Medford Community Media as well as the Tufts provided links.

346
00:37:58,516 --> 00:37:59,336
[SPEAKER_03]: That's all I have.

347
00:37:59,537 --> 00:38:02,118
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm here to answer questions if the community has any.

348
00:38:02,498 --> 00:38:03,198
[SPEAKER_03]: And again, thank you.

349
00:38:05,753 --> 00:38:09,794
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, Victor, appreciate you sharing that on the city's channels.

350
00:38:09,854 --> 00:38:13,315
[SPEAKER_04]: We do have one more question that came in while you were speaking.

351
00:38:13,335 --> 00:38:16,996
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm going to ask John H. to answer this one.

352
00:38:17,937 --> 00:38:19,497
[SPEAKER_04]: This comes from Charles McCabe.

353
00:38:20,418 --> 00:38:23,018
[SPEAKER_04]: The water table in this area is high.

354
00:38:23,118 --> 00:38:31,941
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm concerned that the fields are four feet higher than Fleming Street and Windsor Road, which could cause problems with water runoff.

355
00:38:32,441 --> 00:38:34,622
[SPEAKER_04]: What are the guarantees that this won't happen?

356
00:38:39,455 --> 00:38:40,515
[SPEAKER_02]: Thanks Marco.

357
00:38:40,575 --> 00:38:49,618
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes, so we we've been working on the design of the drainage associated with the tennis courts, the tennis courts will drain to a closed drainage system.

358
00:38:50,158 --> 00:38:59,641
[SPEAKER_02]: So it will not just shut off all four sides of the of the court and make its way make its way to wherever it would go.

359
00:39:00,361 --> 00:39:04,382
[SPEAKER_02]: We do have a closed drainage system where it will capture all the water that actually

360
00:39:05,373 --> 00:39:24,142
[SPEAKER_02]: falls onto the core into a closed drainage system and then into an underground retention system that will hold back a specified volume of water to control all volume and flow from this site.

361
00:39:24,463 --> 00:39:33,467
[SPEAKER_02]: And per our discussions with Medford, in regards to this project and other projects on this site,

362
00:39:34,841 --> 00:39:43,506
[SPEAKER_02]: we will be storing the water to accommodate volume and flow.

363
00:39:43,947 --> 00:40:00,338
[SPEAKER_02]: So per DEP, you know, we have to control flow, but in addition, you know, Medford has requested that we control volume as well, which puts a very sizable underground storage retention tank

364
00:40:00,890 --> 00:40:13,133
[SPEAKER_02]: at the south end of the tennis courts, which is currently in the design and to accommodate those drainage concerns and the predetermined storms.

365
00:40:14,493 --> 00:40:14,973
[SPEAKER_02]: Thanks, Rocco.

366
00:40:16,034 --> 00:40:16,894
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, John.

367
00:40:17,274 --> 00:40:23,556
[SPEAKER_04]: And I think this next one is for you as well, if you don't mind helping us out on this one.

368
00:40:24,056 --> 00:40:28,977
[SPEAKER_04]: How long will it take for the trees you plant to look like the photos that you've showed us?

369
00:40:30,105 --> 00:40:36,588
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, so we're still working through that with the university on how large the trees and the plantings will be.

370
00:40:37,628 --> 00:40:50,814
[SPEAKER_02]: As Janet indicated or alluded to in the discussion of those images, that it's somewhat budget-driven, but the goal, again, out of Rocco's office was to make this corner better.

371
00:40:51,474 --> 00:40:57,837
[SPEAKER_02]: And we want to put as large a trees that we can actually get here economically,

372
00:40:58,717 --> 00:41:07,260
[SPEAKER_02]: as well as shrubs to shield this corner of the facility, but still allow the access to the quarters.

373
00:41:07,380 --> 00:41:22,524
[SPEAKER_02]: So I think the desire to know exactly right now how big they will be that has not been designed as to the maturity or the size of the trees to date, we're still working through that with budgetary concerns.

374
00:41:23,335 --> 00:41:44,704
[SPEAKER_02]: But the goal and the design criteria is to shield it to the best of the ability of the project budget, while also thinking five to 10 years ahead of how big these trees and shrubs are going to get that would shield the facility, but also not affect the playability of the facility.

375
00:41:44,804 --> 00:41:46,844
[SPEAKER_02]: So all of that is in play.

376
00:41:47,645 --> 00:41:48,065
[SPEAKER_04]: Thanks, Rocco.

377
00:41:49,917 --> 00:41:50,738
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you, John.

378
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:55,522
[SPEAKER_04]: And thank you to all of our presenters tonight.

379
00:41:55,622 --> 00:42:00,566
[SPEAKER_04]: And again, thank you to Mark and Andy for their work behind the scenes to make this happen.

380
00:42:00,606 --> 00:42:04,169
[SPEAKER_04]: And for Victor from the city of Medford for joining us tonight.

381
00:42:04,949 --> 00:42:12,816
[SPEAKER_04]: We really do appreciate the feedback that you've given us, but please don't hesitate to call or email us at our office at any time.

382
00:42:13,376 --> 00:42:16,499
[SPEAKER_04]: If you have other thoughts or if there are other neighbors that couldn't make it tonight,

383
00:42:17,740 --> 00:42:22,342
[SPEAKER_04]: Questions or discussions, again, our phone number is 617-627-3780.

384
00:42:22,382 --> 00:42:30,445
[SPEAKER_04]: And we can be reached at communityrelations at tufts.edu via email.

385
00:42:31,185 --> 00:42:35,807
[SPEAKER_04]: Thank you all for joining us tonight, taking the time out of your day to hear more about our project.

386
00:42:36,388 --> 00:42:38,068
[SPEAKER_04]: And we look forward to working with you.

387
00:42:38,328 --> 00:42:43,010
[SPEAKER_04]: And we look forward to seeing our neighbors out there on the tennis courts on nights like this.

388
00:42:43,650 --> 00:42:45,971
[SPEAKER_04]: So thank you all very much and have a good evening.

389
00:42:45,991 --> 00:42:47,372
[SPEAKER_04]: Thanks, everybody.

